From: djsaunde <1245942+djsaunde@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/21] fast: draw nothing for a reversed TEXRECT / FILLRECT,
 as the RDP does

The RDP's rectangle commands carry their corners as unsigned 12-bit
U10.2 fields. When the lower-right corner lies above or left of the
upper-left one, the edge walker finds no scanline (y) or marks every
span as crossed (x), and nothing is drawn. Games rely on this: 1080
Snowboarding's snowfall writes each flake's corners with `(x << 2) &
0xFFF`, so a flake whose corner went one pixel off the left or top edge
wraps to ~1023 and is dropped by the hardware.

Fast3D drew such a rectangle as a quad between the two corners, so the
dropped flake became a rectangle over the whole screen with its 8x8
texture repeating across it: a regular grid of soft dots (found against n64ref).
Return early from GfxDpTextureRectangle and GfxDpFillRectangle when
lrx < ulx or lry < uly. Ordered rectangles are unchanged.
---
 src/fast/interpreter.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
index 4078a5c..24fc3c5 100644
--- a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
@@ -3083,6 +3083,13 @@ void Interpreter::GfxDrawRectangle(int32_t ulx, int32_t uly, int32_t lrx, int32_
 void Interpreter::GfxDpTextureRectangle(int32_t ulx, int32_t uly, int32_t lrx, int32_t lry, uint8_t tile, int16_t uls,
                                         int16_t ult, int16_t dsdx, int16_t dtdy, bool flip) {
     // printf("render %d at %d\n", tile, lrx);
+    // The RDP draws nothing when the lower-right corner is above or left of the upper-left one
+    // (its edge walker finds no scanline, or every span crosses). Games rely on that: a sprite
+    // whose corner went negative is wrapped by the 12-bit U10.2 fields to ~1023 and so dropped.
+    // Drawn as a quad it would span the whole screen, its texture repeating across it.
+    if (lrx < ulx || lry < uly) {
+        return;
+    }
     uint64_t saved_combine_mode = mRdp->combine_mode;
     if ((mRdp->other_mode_h & (3U << G_MDSFT_CYCLETYPE)) == G_CYC_COPY) {
         // Per RDP Command Summary Set Tile's shift s and this dsdx should be set to 4 texels
@@ -3199,6 +3206,10 @@ void Interpreter::GfxDpImageRectangle(int32_t tile, int32_t w, int32_t h, int32_
 }
 
 void Interpreter::GfxDpFillRectangle(int32_t ulx, int32_t uly, int32_t lrx, int32_t lry) {
+    // A reversed rectangle is empty on the RDP (see GfxDpTextureRectangle).
+    if (lrx < ulx || lry < uly) {
+        return;
+    }
     if (mRdp->color_image_address == mRdp->z_buf_address) {
         // Fullscreen Z clears are redundant — already done by glClear at frame start.
         bool isFullScreen = (ulx <= 0 && uly <= 0 && lrx >= (int32_t)(mNativeDimensions.width - 1) * 4 &&
